  "tickets": [
    {
      "id": 5,
      "title": "MCP for PM",
      "body": "Description pending",
      "status": "done",
      "priority": "high",
      "labels": [
        "mcp"
      ],
      "assignee": null,
      "author": "",
      "created": 1788448748,
      "updated": 1788495377,
      "anchors": [],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788481882,
          "body": "So MCP for PM is needed. The goal for PM is to be more of a diff based review annotate and ticketing way of vibecoding rather than just pure prompting so it's like,,, i hate the word,,, second brain. But the goal is for pm to have an mcp crate and have a stdio mcp that allows it to list projects, open up a project in the pm, list tickets, comment on tickets, read on tickets. Solving this base PM-5 needs to solve PM-15 first.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788483066,
          "body": "MCP server shipped as crates/pm-mcp (rmcp 3.2, stdio). Works directly on .pm/pm.json5 via pm-core (no GUI needed); project chosen by --project / positional / cwd, with per-call project override that walks up to the nearest .pm/. Tools: list_tickets, get_ticket, add_comment, create_ticket, edit_ticket, open_project (spawns the pm GUI), list_projects (dir scan). .mcp.json at the repo root registers it with Claude Code. This comment was posted through pm-mcp itself. Depends on PM-15 (author), also in_progress.",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "author": "reaganiwadha",
          "created": 1788486266,
          "body": "We need MCP Installer. install.ps1 installs the pm binary yes, but we should have a subcommand named `pm setup`. Actually let's change the cli syntax to be `pm .` to open this project `pm` just opens pm without specifying directory, `pm --mcp` to run mcp `pm --setup` is the first thing the install.ps1 launches. and in this pm --setup, it asks whether to associate itself/add itself in the menu, register like windows application registry properly, register an uninstaller so it shows up in the bcuninstaller/windows uninstall thingy. and more importantly, pm --setup has an mcp configurator/mcp plugger. Find like a repository where it has an mcp plugger that detects claude code or something and plugs itself properly. Target claude code first",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "author": "unknown",
          "created": 1788495095,
          "body": "Closed, MCP primitives is there now",
          "anchor": null
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788495377,
          "body": "Done. Recap of everything shipped for this ticket:\n\n- crates/pm-mcp — rmcp 3.2 stdio server; tools list_tickets / get_ticket / add_comment / create_ticket / edit_ticket / open_project / list_projects. Works directly on .pm/pm.json5 via pm-core.\n- CLI reshaped to flags (hard switch): `pm` = \"Nothing opened\" screen, `pm .` / `pm <path>` = GUI, `pm --mcp [--project p]`, `pm --setup [--yes]`, `pm --uninstall [--yes]`, `pm --update`.\n- `pm --setup` (crates/pm-core/src/setup.rs, Windows): figlet banner + plain y/n prompts; reg.exe writes App Paths + Uninstall keys (pm shows in \"Installed apps\" / BCUninstaller, UninstallString = \"<exe>\" --uninstall --yes); ensures install dir on PATH; optional Start Menu .lnk; MCP plugger targets Claude Code — `claude mcp add pm -s user -- pm --mcp` if the CLI is present, else edits ~/.claude.json mcpServers.pm.\n- `pm --uninstall` reverses all of it and self-deletes.\n- install.ps1 runs `pm --setup` after install; repo .mcp.json uses `cargo run -q -p pm -- --mcp`.\n\nFollow-ups worth their own tickets: MCP plugger support for Cursor / Windsurf; `pm --setup` on macOS/Linux (currently Windows-only, bails elsewhere).",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ]
    },
