        {
          "id": 1,
          "author": "claude",
          "created": 1788495425,
          "body": "Partial. Done: Ticket.author / Comment.author (free, unverified strings), Config.author (~/.pm/config.json), pm_core::resolve_author(explicit → config → git user.name → \"unknown\"), the GUI \"as:\" author_box in the Tickets pane, and per-action Option<String> overrides in create_ticket / add_comment (MCP tools take `author`).\n\nNot done: a first-class \"who am I\" control. PM-56 covers that (footer user section, git-username default). Also a bug to fix there: a non-git pm window resolves author to \"unknown\" and the ticket-submit path then persists that into the shared config, poisoning attribution for every project — the default should come from git user.name and only be written to config on an explicit user action.",
          "anchor": null
        }
      ]
    },
